{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-118734",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Note, that the full angle is the sum of the measure of interior angles of an equilateral triangle, a regular octagon, a regular pentagon, and the measure of the shaded angle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14193755/assets/1289ebe280e4fc07cc71a7f45a8660c6ce29fb367567f07e1efb4d3712cbe767.png)\n\n \n\nFor a regular polygon with $n$ sides, the  measure of each interior angle must be\n\n$$\n\\frac{{180}^{∘}\\cdot (n-2)}{n}.\n$$\n\n \n\n In an equilateral triangle, there are $3$ equivalent interior angles, so each has a measure of \n\n$$\n\\frac{{180}^{∘}(3-2)}{3}={60}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, in a regular octagon, there are $8$ equivalent interior angles, so each has a measure of \n\n$$\n\\frac{{180}^{∘}(8-2)}{8}={135}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nA regular pentagon has $5$ equivalent interior angles, so each has a measure of \n\n$$\n\\frac{{180}^{∘}(5-2)}{5}={108}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nLet us call $x$ the measure of the shaded angle. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{60}^{∘}+{135}^{∘}+{108}^{∘}+x & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ {303}^{∘}+x & ={360}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={57}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-118734\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>Note, that the full angle is the sum of the measure of interior angles of an equilateral triangle, a regular octagon, a regular pentagon, and the measure of the shaded angle.</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-b0e93fd4f653d211d57bfc9989fbde18\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/b0e93fd4f653d211d57bfc9989fbde18\"></div> \n\n<p>For a regular polygon with <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"21\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45B TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> sides, the  measure of each interior angle must be\n<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" display=\"true\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"22\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math display=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"margin-left: 0px; margin-right: 0px;\"><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mfrac><mjx-frac type=\"d\"><mjx-num><mjx-nstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-nstrut><mjx-mrow><mjx-msup><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c38\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: 0.393em;\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2218\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-script></mjx-msup><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c22C5\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c28\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45B TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2212\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"3\"><mjx-c class=